{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504116,"name":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","username":"zdfs","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/zdfs/{size}/101520_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T16:32:01.231Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSomewhere else…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA shared canvas opened in a browser (Chrome, signed in, at \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases\u003c/a\u003e) shows only the top of the canvas. The mouse wheel, trackpad, scrollbar, and Page Down do nothing. The same canvas scrolls normally when opened inside the Cursor editor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe page itself has no scrollable overflow: document scrollHeight equals the viewport height. This is the \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e shared-canvas viewer, which is why the product is “Somewhere else” rather than the IDE.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a canvas whose content is taller than the browser window.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePublish it and open the share link in Chrome while signed in: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=\u003c/a\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTry to scroll with the mouse wheel, trackpad, or Page Down.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResult: the view stays on the first screen. There is no scrollbar, and the wheel does nothing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe canvas content scrolls, or the page grows to the height the iframe already reports via cursor-shared-canvas-resize. A reader should be able to reach the bottom of a shared canvas in the browser the same way they can in the editor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor IDE 3.22.12 (Electron 42.10.0, Chromium 148.0.7778.280). The canvas scrolls correctly inside the editor. The failure is on \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e in Chrome, checked 30 Sep 2026. macOS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI checked the forum first. Nothing matches this. Nearby reports are different: a standalone IDE canvas window going unresponsive (topic 166875), published canvas links needing a modified click (169468), /api/canvas-frame returning 404 (169974), and the IDE canvas max-width change (159574).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat the live viewer does:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe canvas is a sandboxed iframe at /api/canvas-frame/?theme=dark. The sandbox is “allow-scripts allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox” (no allow-same-origin).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe shell is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e[data-shared-canvas-overlay]: position fixed, inset-x-0, top-0, z-index 100, flex column, overflow hidden, height 100dvh\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e[data-shared-canvas-body]: relative, min-height 0, flex-1, overflow hidden\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eiframe[data-shared-canvas-frame]: width 100%, height 100%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a short window the iframe box was about 297px tall, and the parent document’s scrollHeight equaled its clientHeight, so a wheel on the page has nothing to move.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe iframe posts a cursor-shared-canvas-resize message with a height. The viewer writes that only to the CSS variable --shared-canvas-print-height, and the stylesheet applies it only inside \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@media\u003c/span\u003e print:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e[data-shared-canvas-frame] { height: var(–shared-canvas-print-height, 100vh) !important; }\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn screen the iframe stays height 100%. Forcing the iframe to 5000px made the resize message report 5048 (the iframe height plus the host’s 48px of body padding) and the rest of the canvas was visible below the fold. The content is intact. The viewer never gives it a scrollable box.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis showed up after the 3.22 canvas host update (3.21.18, then 3.22.7 on 22 Sep, then 3.22.12 on 26 Sep). A shared canvas first failed to scroll in Chrome on 28 Sep. The editor webview still scrolls.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA second issue on the same page: an open modal set pointer-events: none on body, while the canvas overlay sits above it at z-index 100, so wheel events pass through the iframe onto the backdrop. Closing that modal does not fix the clipping. The shell is still overflow hidden and the iframe is still height 100%.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuggested fix: on screen, size the iframe from cursor-shared-canvas-resize (the same height already used for print) and let the page scroll. Or give the iframe a viewport-sized box and let the canvas document inside it scroll.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504116-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504116-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T18:40:38.068Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":30.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":173424,"topic_slug":"shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser","display_username":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"http://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":105648,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser/173424/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":504159,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T17:24:25.386Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/zdfs\"\u003e@zdfs\u003c/a\u003e Thanks for the post! I tried to reproduce this bug but I couldn’t reproduce it as you’ve experienced it. On \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e the page itself is meant to stay fixed; the canvas scrolls inside its own frame. We tried the same layout with a tall canvas and it scrolls there, so we think something on the page is blocking input to the canvas. The dialog you noticed is our main suspect.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you try this and tell us what happens?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClose every other \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e tab.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the share link in a new tab and do a hard reload (Cmd+Shift+R).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDon’t open any menus or dialogs on the page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMove the mouse over the canvas and scroll with the wheel or trackpad.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf that doesn’t scroll, click once inside the canvas and press Page Down.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDoes it scroll at step 4 or step 5? a screenshot would be helpful too!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the meantime, “Download as PDF” in the canvas header gives you the whole canvas, and it still scrolls normally in the editor.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T17:24:25.386Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173424,"topic_slug":"shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser/173424/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":504194,"name":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","username":"zdfs","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/zdfs/{size}/101520_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T18:38:03.404Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/kevinn\"\u003e@kevinn\u003c/a\u003e, thanks. I followed the steps exactly: one \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e tab, share link in a new tab, Cmd+Shift+R, no menus or dialogs opened.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStep 4: does not scroll. Step 5: does not scroll. The header does not take clicks either, so Download as PDF, Open in full screen and Copy link all do nothing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevTools on the freshly loaded page shows why input is dead. A Radix dialog (\u003ccode\u003ediv[role=\"dialog\"]#radix-…\u003c/code\u003e) opens on its own as soon as the canvas finishes loading: \u003cstrong\u003eGrok Bot Terms\u003c/strong\u003e, with \u003cstrong\u003eNot now\u003c/strong\u003e (focused) and \u003cstrong\u003eAccept and Continue\u003c/strong\u003e. It sits at \u003ccode\u003ez-index: 50\u003c/code\u003e with a full-viewport \u003ccode\u003e.fixed.inset-0.z-50.bg-black/50\u003c/code\u003e backdrop. The shared-canvas shell is \u003ccode\u003efixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-[100]\u003c/code\u003e with an opaque background, so the dialog is never visible. While it is open, \u003ccode\u003ebody\u003c/code\u003e is \u003ccode\u003epointer-events: none\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eoverflow: hidden\u003c/code\u003e, and the shell inherits that. \u003ccode\u003edocument.elementsFromPoint\u003c/code\u003e at the center of each header button returns the backdrop \u003ccode\u003eDIV\u003c/code\u003e, not the button. Wheel events over the canvas land on the same backdrop.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClicking \u003cstrong\u003eNot now\u003c/strong\u003e (or pressing Enter, since it has focus) removes the dialog, \u003ccode\u003ebody\u003c/code\u003e goes back to \u003ccode\u003epointer-events: auto\u003c/code\u003e, and the PDF button becomes the hit target. A reload brings the dialog back. This is an org-level terms prompt, so an account that has already accepted it will not see the problem, which would explain why your tall canvas scrolled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo this thread has two things:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe hidden dialog above, which blocks all input on the page for anyone who has not accepted the prompt. The canvas shell should not paint over a modal, or the modal should not open on the shared-canvas route.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe sizing question from my first post (iframe fixed at viewport height, page has no overflow). I will confirm whether the frame scrolls once the dialog is dismissed and report back.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShare link (signed-in view): \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=canvas-hQNdNxqSCKkXX02rRCuJr1MX\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=canvas-hQNdNxqSCKkXX02rRCuJr1MX\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T18:38:03.404Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173424,"topic_slug":"shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser","display_username":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/dashboard/shared-canvases?shareId=canvas-hQNdNxqSCKkXX02rRCuJr1MX","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":105648,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser/173424/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":504197,"name":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","username":"zdfs","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/zdfs/{size}/101520_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T18:40:33.389Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI ended up using DevTools to increase the zIndex and accepted the terms and now things work normally.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T18:40:33.389Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":10.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173424,"topic_slug":"shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser","display_username":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[{"badges":[{"id":112,"name":"Checkpoint Restored","description":"Solved their own issue and came back to share","grant_count":383,"allow_title":false,"multiple_grant":true,"icon":"check","image_url":null,"listable":true,"enabled":true,"badge_grouping_id":6,"system":false,"slug":"checkpoint-restored","manually_grantable":true,"show_in_post_header":true,"badge_type_id":3}],"badge_types":[{"id":3,"name":"Bronze","sort_order":7}],"basic_user_badge":{"id":161417,"granted_at":"2026-09-30T18:47:54.842Z","grouping_position":0,"badge_id":112}}],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":105648,"username":"zdfs","name":"Zachary Forrest y Salazar","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/zdfs/{size}/101520_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":105648,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/shared-canvases-do-not-scroll-in-the-browser/173424/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":504206,"name":"Kev